  "summary": "Monday 10/26 St. Brigid CT list prepared per RBC-RAD-07. 4 booked studies; 3 cancelled appointments (pt-0048, pt-0012, pt-0050) excluded.\n\n1) pt-0047 Britt Mohr, CT A/P w/ contrast 08:00 (sr-t0001, appt-00005): no contrast reaction; diabetes (diet); creatinine 9/24 outside 30 days -> pre-scan creatinine ordered (sr-t0005). Late outside creatinine 1.52 (10/22, eGFR ~64, not AKI by policy definition) -> decisions unchanged; follow-up task t0032. Patient instructions comm-t0013.\n\n2) pt-0015 Daniel Ferreira, CT A/P w/ contrast 09:00 (sr-t0002, appt-00003): 2019 reaction graded MODERATE by the radiology report of that day (allergy list says \"anaphylaxis, patient report\") -> prednisone 50 mg 20:00/02:00/08:00 (mr-t0003) + diphenhydramine 50 mg 08:00 (mr-t0004); needs a driver. Corrected creatinine arrived (2.8, not 0.98; eGFR ~24) -> added NaCl 0.9% 500 mL IV at 08:00 (mr-t0021). Instructions in Spanish/English (comm-t0014) plus correction (comm-t0025); follow-up task t0031 for the new kidney finding.\n\n3) pt-0049 Anisha Schuster, CT A/P w/ contrast 13:00 (sr-t0006, appt-00007): ED AKI 10/04-05 not back to baseline -> pre-scan creatinine (sr-t0007), NaCl 500 mL IV at 12:00 (mr-t0008), metformin on hold (mr-00392), post-scan creatinine 10/28-30 (sr-t0010), restart task t0012. Late outside report showed a moderate iopamidol reaction (2022) -> prednisone 00:00/06:00/12:00 (mr-t0022) + diphenhydramine 12:00 (mr-t0023), driver needed. Instructions comm-t0015 plus correction comm-t0026. Iopamidol could not be added to allergy list (not in catalog) and is flagged in the note.\n\n4) pt-0046 Lauren Beahan, CT A/P without contrast 14:00 (sr-t0011, appt-00004): no prep needed. Late outside report of a mild iohexol reaction added to allergy list (alg-t0024); no change because the study is non-contrast. Instructions comm-t0016.\n\nNotes and addenda written for each patient. The 4 inbox items that arrived during the work were closed. Unrelated older inbox items were left untouched.",
